/-
A vector, a Hilbert space, and the norm, each read on the EKG.

A vector space over the reals with an inner product, complete in the length the inner product gives, is a Hilbert space.
The plane the coins are carried to meets each of those interfaces as Mathlib states them, and the EKG reads what it costs
to see each one met.  Its completeness is free: it is finite.  Then the operator norm of the device's table, and the walls.
-/
import Calibrate.Device
import Calibrate.Norm

namespace Calibrate

ekg_meets (inferInstance : Module ℝ ThePlane)
ekg_meets (inferInstance : InnerProductSpace ℝ ThePlane)
ekg_meets (inferInstance : CompleteSpace ThePlane)
ekg_meets (the_operator_norm_of_the_table : ‖theOperator‖ = 18 + theRoot)
ekg_meets (the_norm_squared_is_between_the_walls : 755 < ‖theOperator‖ ^ 2 ∧ ‖theOperator‖ ^ 2 ≤ 756)

end Calibrate
